The order isomorphism from the elements of a neighbourhood system to the elements of the system reconstructed from a computable presentation sends each element to the filter of hint neighbourhoods of neighbourhoods it contains, and inverts this by collecting the underlying neighbourhoods of the hint neighbourhoods in a reconstructed element. On an original element, equality of hint neighbourhoods is equality of underlying neighbourhoods, and every neighbourhood in the element is enumerated by an index that witnesses the round trip. On a reconstructed element, the same equality identifies a hint neighbourhood with the hint neighbourhood of its index, and every hint neighbourhood in the element is a neighbourhood of the reconstructed system. The approximation order is preserved and reflected because a neighbourhood lies in an element exactly when the hint neighbourhood of an enumerating index lies in the image, and a hint neighbourhood lies in an image exactly when its underlying neighbourhood lies in the original element.
